  "description": "ZOXVOZ crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C206 H142 N46 Nd13 O69 3+,3(N1 O3 1-),10(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Nd1 (Nd) has 12 O neighbors; Nd2 (Nd) has 7 O neighbors; Nd3 (Nd) has 6 O neighbors; Nd4 (Nd) has 7 O neighbors; Nd5 (Nd) has 7 O neighbors; Nd6 (Nd) has 8 O neighbors; Nd7 (Nd) has 7 O neighbors; Nd8 (Nd) has 7 O neighbors; Nd9 (Nd) has 6 O neighbors; Nd10 (Nd) has 8 O neighbors; Nd11 (Nd) has 6 O neighbors; Nd12 (Nd) has 8 O neighbors; Nd13 (Nd) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 33 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 4.213-5.081 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 114.74-169.25°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Nd13(ccnm)4(CO3)14(NO3)4(H2O)7(phen)15](NO3)3·10H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 7 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 3 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
